[the blueprints and every parameter, printed]
    CONFLICT-RING(M, R, sticky, win): brick pairing {(i,i+1): i even} on even blocks, {(i,i+1 mod M): i odd} on odd blocks; sticky = rounds per pairing (0 = never rotate, the delivery-free limit); win in (S, R, ALT).
    Per pair per round: ONE delivery iff the two actors do not already share an unsuperseded base, then TWO opposite proposals, then ONE two-proposer arbitration.  Round 0 needs no delivery (every actor holds genesis v0).
    CONFLICT-GRID(g, R): g x g actors; rounds alternate ROW and COLUMN groups (orthogonal partitions, so no two actors share a group twice running); group seed = the diagonal member; g - 1 deliveries + g proposals + ONE g-proposer arbitration per group per round.
    SKY-B depths measured = (2, 3); committed SKYB_DEPTH = 2.  Full-menu replay budgets: 420s per record, 120s for the wide record.
