[A1(b) THE CONFLICT BUDGET — how much of a record CAN be arbitration?]
  BOUND (a counting theorem of the layer, not a parameter).  An arbitration's
  ckey is a set of k live proposal triples, and a proposal is resolved by at
  most one arbitration in any record (`View.resolved`), so #proposals >= k *
  #arbs and an arbitration's share of the events of a record is at most
  1/(k+1) where k is the smallest proposer count in it.  Deliveries only
  lower it.  The delivery-free CONFLICT-RING(sticky = 0) SATURATES the bound.
    RING(M=4,R=6,sticky=1,win=S)           n=  46 arbs= 12 (k=2) deliveries= 10 arb share 6/23 (~0.2609) vs bound 1/(k+1) = 1/3 (~0.3333)
