  [PASS] A1(b) THE ARBITRATION SHARE IS BOUNDED BY THE GRAMMAR AND THE BOUND IS ATTAINED.  Every proposal in every swept record is consumed by exactly one arbitration (#proposals = sum of proposer counts, gated), so no record of this layer can be more than 1/(k+1) arbitration, and the delivery-free ring attains it exactly at 1/3.  THE DESIGN PROBLEM THE PIN NAMED, MEASURED: re-supplying a conflict costs one delivery per group per round, which is why the rotating ring runs at 25.6% rather than 33.3% — and A2/A3 show what that delivery BUYS  (records checked = 15, proposal-consumption equalities = 15, bound violations = 0, saturating records = ['RING(M=6,R=10,sticky=0,win=S)'])

